course: dictionary
lesson: 15509
title: Submersion: under the water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Submersion is a noun. It means being completely under water or another liquid, or the act of putting something fully under water. Look at the start of the word: sub means under, as in submarine.
explain: «The diver practised submersion in the pool, staying under for one whole minute.» The clues are diver, pool and staying under. Each one points to being fully under the water, so submersion must mean that.
explain: Submersion is not the same as getting wet. «The rain made my coat wet, but it was not submersion.» A coat in the rain is wet on the outside. Submersion means the whole thing goes under the water.
fact: Submersion means being completely under water or another liquid.
fact: Submersion can also mean the act of putting something or someone fully under water.
fact: Submarines control submersion by filling tanks with water, so they can sink under the sea.
fact: Some watches and phones are tested for submersion to check they still work under water.
fact: Drowning can happen quickly and quietly, so swim where there are lifeguards and never swim alone.
exercise: «The submarine began its submersion at dawn.» What does submersion mean here? | Painting its outside | *Going fully under water | Sailing across the sea | Coming up for air
exercise: Ella says submersion means being on top of the water. Is she right? | Yes, it means riding a bike fast | Yes, it means floating on the waves | No, it means being very cold | *No, it means being completely under water
exercise: Why are some watches tested for submersion? | *To check they still work when fully under water | To make them lighter to carry | To see how fast they can run | To make them shine brighter
test: «The watch passed its test for submersion in the tank.» What does submersion mean in this sentence? | Being in bright sunlight | Being shaken very hard | Being carried by a friend | *Being fully under water
test: Which is a safety rule about water submersion? | Swim far from the shore with no one nearby | Swim alone at night when it is quiet | Dive into shallow water without looking | *Swim where there are lifeguards and never swim alone
exam: Which sentence uses submersion correctly? | «He felt submersion when he was happy.» | «She ran submersion around the field.» | *«Some Christians are baptised by full submersion in water.» | «The submersion of the bread was tasty.»
